  "description": "EQUQUG crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C56 H56 Cl2 Gd6 N40 O12,7(C2 H6 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 3 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 4 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 4 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 3 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 4 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.735-4.207 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 103.71-123.66°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd6(OH)6(OC2H5)2(Cl)2(bpmtm)4(H2O)4]·7C2H5OH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
